# FPS Architecture (MVP → Scale)

Design for a small demo first, but keep **clear ownership** so systems can grow independently.

## Suggested responsibilities

| Module | Owns | Does not own |
|--------|------|--------------|
| Player Motor | move, jump, ground check | shooting, UI |
| Camera / Look | aim, sensitivity | weapon logic |
| Weapon | fire, reload, ammo, hitscan/projectile | player movement |
| Health / Damage | hp, death, damage apply | VFX presentation details |
| UI | HUD bind to state | gameplay rules |

## Rules of thumb

- A weapon should not move the player; the player should not draw the HUD directly inside fire logic
- Tunable values (spread, RPM, damage, FOV, move speed…) live **only** in ScriptableObjects under `Assets/Data/`
- Hitscan/aim logic returns a result (`HitResult`); VFX/audio react to that result
- Keep networking/multiplayer hooks **out** until needed — but avoid writing code that hard-locks to a single MonoBehaviour singleton for core combat

## Scaling path (when the demo grows)

1. Add/extend SO configs first when balancing grows (new weapons = new SO assets, same type)
2. Introduce a thin `IDamageable` (or similar) before adding many damage sources
3. Add state only when modes appear (menu, playing, paused, dead) — not before
